            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A chair includes a seat, a backrest separated from the seat, and an upper support frame to which the backrest is rotatably attached at a position higher than the seat. In the chair, the upper support frame includes a left side portion and a right side portions both extending forward at left and right sides of the seated person and a rear portion that continuously and integrally connects the left side portion and the right side portion. The left side portion and the right side portion are connected to side support bodies arranged on left and right sides of the seat to be tiltable, and the backrest is connected to the upper support frame at a position lower than an upper-lower intermediate position of the backrest to be tiltable rearward.</p>
            </abstract>
